From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: make the mesh peerings again after a hardware restart

A driver calls ieee80211_hw_restart_disconnect() when its firmware did
not carry a station's connection over a restart: mac80211 then
disconnects and userspace connects again. A mesh interface had no such
path. mac80211 adds its peers back after the restart as if nothing had
happened, but a firmware that numbers the protected frames from zero
again leaves every peer dropping our frames as replays, and nothing
acts on that: the link stays "established" and carries no traffic
(seen with ath11k on IPQ5018/QCN6122, SAE mesh: the peer's replay
counter grows, no ping comes back).

Let a driver call ieee80211_hw_restart_disconnect() for a mesh
interface too. mac80211 then removes the peers once the restart is
done. With the kernel MPM that closes the links (mesh_sta_cleanup()
sends the CLOSE) and the peers are found again from their beacons. A
userspace MPM sees the stations go (NL80211_CMD_DEL_STATION), closes
the links and makes them again. The keys of a mesh interface are not
tainted: the beacon and the group-addressed frames go on with them
while the peerings are made again.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/net/mac80211/util.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/util.c
@@ -2383,6 +2383,8 @@
 				continue;
 			if (sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION)
 				ieee80211_sta_restart(sdata);
+			else if (ieee80211_vif_is_mesh(&sdata->vif))
+				ieee80211_mesh_restart(sdata);
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -2442,11 +2444,19 @@
 		    !local->in_reconfig))
 		return;
 
-	if (WARN_ON(vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION))
+	if (WARN_ON(vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION &&
+		    vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT))
 		return;
 
 	sdata->flags |= flag;
 
+	/* A mesh interface keeps its keys: its peerings are made again
+	 * with new ones, and the beacon and the group-addressed frames
+	 * go on meanwhile.
+	 */
+	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT)
+		return;
+
 	list_for_each_entry(key, &sdata->key_list, list)
 		key->flags |= KEY_FLAG_TAINTED;
 }
--- a/net/mac80211/mesh_plink.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mesh_plink.c
@@ -387,6 +387,33 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * ieee80211_mesh_restart - make the peerings again after a hardware restart
+ *
+ * @sdata: mesh interface the driver called ieee80211_hw_restart_disconnect() for
+ *
+ * The driver could not carry the peerings over the restart: typically its
+ * firmware numbers the frames it protects from zero again, so every peer
+ * drops what we send as a replay. Remove the peers. With the kernel MPM
+ * that closes the links (mesh_sta_cleanup()) and the peers are found again
+ * from their beacons. A userspace MPM sees the stations go
+ * (NL80211_CMD_DEL_STATION), closes the links itself and makes them again.
+ */
+void ieee80211_mesh_restart(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata)
+{
+	lockdep_assert_wiphy(sdata->local->hw.wiphy);
+
+	if (!(sdata->flags & IEEE80211_SDATA_DISCONNECT_HW_RESTART))
+		return;
+	sdata->flags &= ~IEEE80211_SDATA_DISCONNECT_HW_RESTART;
+
+	if (!sdata->u.mesh.mesh_id_len)
+		return;
+
+	mpl_dbg(sdata, "driver requested new peerings after hardware restart\n");
+	sta_info_flush(sdata, -1);
+}
+
+/**
  * mesh_plink_deactivate - deactivate mesh peer link
  *
  * @sta: mesh peer link to deactivate
--- a/net/mac80211/mesh.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/mesh.h
@@ -340,6 +340,7 @@
 u64 mesh_accept_plinks_update(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata);
 void mesh_plink_timer(struct timer_list *t);
 void mesh_plink_broken(struct sta_info *sta);
+void ieee80211_mesh_restart(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata);
 u64 mesh_plink_deactivate(struct sta_info *sta);
 u64 mesh_plink_open(struct sta_info *sta);
 u64 mesh_plink_block(struct sta_info *sta);
--- a/include/net/mac80211.h
+++ b/include/net/mac80211.h
@@ -7172,7 +7172,10 @@
  * @vif: &struct ieee80211_vif pointer from the add_interface callback.
  *
  * Instructs mac80211 to disconnect from the AP after
- * hardware restart.
+ * hardware restart. On a mesh interface it instructs mac80211 to drop
+ * the peerings, which are then made again; a driver calls it when its
+ * firmware did not carry the peers' state (packet numbers, ...) over
+ * the restart.
  */
 void ieee80211_hw_restart_disconnect(struct ieee80211_vif *vif);
 
